new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a5d63b3d58fdfdb2e663309b59decef1b84ca1e9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test-apps/r0-multiprocess-probe/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# R0 multiprocess probe app
+
+Source-controlled ordinary multiprocess fixture for P5 device acceptance.
+
+Contract:
+
+- Package: `com.r0dump.multiprocess`.
+- Exported launcher: `MainActivity`.
+- `MainActivity` starts non-exported `ChildService` in process `:child`.
+- `MainActivity` and `ChildService` each run 64 file-backed `DexFile` open/close cycles and
+  64 short-lived `DexClassLoader` loads, then load their own primary DEX once through a
+  `ByteBuffer`-backed `InMemoryDexClassLoader`. Each process reports one
+  `cookie_churn_complete dex_file=64 class_loader=64 in_memory=1` result.
+- Deterministic descriptor targets: `MainTarget` and `ChildTarget`.
+- Exact force-invoke target:
+  `Lcom/r0dump/multiprocess/r0dump_ForceInvokeTarget;->r0dump_materializeOnly()V`.
+  It is not referenced during ordinary app startup. Its `<clinit>` increments only the external
+  `clinit` counter; a real dispatch of the target method increments `dispatch`.
+- The exported query receiver is intentionally independent of the target, so it can inspect either
+  counter without initializing the target class.
+- No ART/runtime production files or dependencies.
+
+Build:
+
+```sh
+./test-apps/r0-multiprocess-probe/build.sh
+```
+
+Install and run fresh device acceptance:
+
+```sh
+./test-apps/r0-multiprocess-probe/run-acceptance.sh f5e3adbc
+```
+
+Force-invoke fixture query (after an independent app process is started for the configured run):
+
+```sh
+adb shell am broadcast -a com.r0dump.multiprocess.action.R0DUMP_FORCE_INVOKE_QUERY \
+  -n com.r0dump.multiprocess/.r0dump_ForceInvokeProbeReceiver
+adb logcat -d -s R0ForceInvokeFixture:I '*:S'
+```
+
+The stable result is `clinit=<n> dispatch=<n>`. A force-invoke run must report `clinit=1` and
+`dispatch=0`; a disabled/no-target run must report `clinit=0 dispatch=0`. Querying itself must not
+change either counter.
+
+The runner preserves app data, snapshots/restores touched r0dump props, clears only this
+package's r0dump output, validates isolated main/child sessions, runs `dexdump` on standard DEX
+artifacts, checks both target descriptors, and stops the app on exit. VCB/MT non-spawn is
+inconclusive external-app behavior and is not an r0dump failure.
diff --git a/test-apps/r0-multiprocess-probe/build.sh b/test-apps/r0-multiprocess-probe/build.sh
