index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..20ed46ddba1a94d07ba70fa3d57e112af8f1465c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test-apps/v31-probe/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+# V3.2 controlled probe app
+
+`ProbeTarget#probe():int` is a static, no-argument, side-effect-free method with more than eight
+DEX instructions. `ProbeActivity` initializes it on the normal app path before `ActivityThread`
+starts the V3.1 worker.
+
+Build and install:
+
+```sh
+./test-apps/v31-probe/build.sh
+adb -s <serial> install -r test-apps/v31-probe/r0-v31-probe.apk
+```
+
+Run the bounded probe ladder:
+
+```sh
+./test-apps/v31-probe/run-ladder.sh <serial>
+```
+
+## F7 ClassLoader walk fixture
+
+`r0dump_LoadedTarget` is initialized by `ProbeActivity.onCreate()` before the
+`after_first_activity_on_create` walk trigger. `r0dump_UninitializedSentinel` is present in the
+same DEX, but no ordinary startup or query path names or loads it. Its static initializer is the
+only code that increments `sentinel_init`.
+
+After launching the activity, query state with the exported, read-only receiver:
+
+```sh
+adb -s <serial> shell am broadcast \
+  -a com.r0dump.v31.action.R0DUMP_WALK_STATE \
+  -n com.r0dump.v31/.r0dump_WalkStateReceiver
+adb -s <serial> logcat -d -s R0WalkFixture:I '*:S'
+```
+
+The stable result is `generation=<n> loaded_init=1 sentinel_init=0`. Repeat the broadcast before
+and after collecting a run: it must not change either counter. Configure F7 with
+`walk_start=after_first_activity_on_create`, `walk_enabled=true`, bits 39 and 40, and one run at a
+time for each mode:
+
+- `walk_mode=loaded_only`: records for `r0dump_LoadedTarget` must use the loaded lookup lane, and
+  `sentinel_init` remains `0`.
+- `walk_mode=dex_names`: records for `r0dump_UninitializedSentinel` must use the
+  `Class.forName(name, false, loader)` lane. It may materialize class metadata and declared
+  executables, but `sentinel_init` remains `0` because this is not class initialization.
+
+The two runs must use distinct `run_id` values. This fixture deliberately does not configure or
+inspect r0dump output itself; the device acceptance harness owns configuration and artifact
+verification.
+
+The ladder requires the custom ART/framework build and verifies budgets `0, 1, 2, 4, 8`. Every
+run must log the exact stop count and identical before/after code-item fingerprints. The runner
+disables V3 execution properties when it completes.
+
+## V3.2 evidence
+
+`ProbeTarget#nestedProbe():int` is a second static, no-argument, side-effect-free target. With
+budget `1`, V3.2 must stop at the target's `invoke-static` boundary *before* it can enter
+`nestedLeaf()`. This proves an mterp nested call cannot bypass the global execution bound.
+
+After a V3 run, wait at least 10 seconds for Phase3's quiet-period writer and inspect:
+
+```sh
+adb -s <serial> shell 'cat /sdcard/Download/r0dump/com.r0dump.v31/session-*/execute-*/phase3-methods.tsv'
+```
+
+The `probe():int` record must classify as `no-change` with `retain-phase2-output`; the nested run
+must report `v3_stop_scope=target` and name `nestedProbe` in `v3_stopped_method`. A write monitor
+reported as `unmonitored` is deliberate evidence that this APK mapping was not safely eligible for
+page protection, not a claim that no write was possible.
